--- Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org> wrote:

> On Thu, 12 Jun 2008 13:41:45 -0700 (PDT)
> Benjamin Kidwell <benjkidwell@yahoo.com> wrote:
> >   LD      .tmp_vmlinux1
> > mm/built-in.o: In function `__munlock_vma_pages_range':
> > mlock.c:(.text+0x11567): undefined reference to `walk_page_range'
> > make[1]: *** [.tmp_vmlinux1] Error 1
> > make: *** [sub-make] Error 2
> 
> Please send the offending .config.  Be sure to Cc Rik :)
> 
Two things follow: the output of diff badconfig goodconfig, and the output of
grep "=[y|m]" badconfig. I had two machines fail to make with the above
output. This config info is from the core2duo imac box, if the other config
from the P4 (the one that generated the BUG after a successful build) is
relevant I can send that one around too. After some experimentation I got a
successful make on each machine, and I think the key option that enabled a
succesful build was re-enabling CONFIG_PROC_PAGE_MONITOR. Every build with it
not set failed on both machines for me.

